<title>USA: K-Tron Q1 revs down, but net, shr rise.</title>
<headline>K-Tron Q1 revs down, but net, shr rise.</headline>
<dateline>PITMAN, N.J. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Dollars in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>							Three Months Ended</p>
<p>					    Mar 29,		 Mar 30,</p>
<p>						 1997		   1996</p>
<p> Revenues				 $21,344		 $23,579</p>
<p> Operating Income			 1,679		   1,808</p>
<p> Interest expense			   314		     596</p>
<p> Income before income taxes	   1,365		   1,212</p>
<p> Income taxes				 315		     460</p>
<p> Net Income				 1,050		     752</p>
<p> Earnings per share			 .33		     .24</p>
<p>Average number of common and common</p>
<p>equivalent shares outstanding</p>
<p>					  3,182,000	     3,127,000</p>
<p>NOTES: The company said revenues fell 10 percent, from $23.6 million to $21.3 million, attributable to conversion of foreign revenue into U.S. dollars at lower exchange rates. If foreign currency exchange rates remained consistent between periods, revenues would have risen slightly and net would have been greater.</p>
<p>Full company name is K-Tron International Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
